<% title 'Privacy Policy' %>

<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

<p>This policy covers the Blitzen Trapper website and forum at forum.blitzentrapper.net.</p>

<h2>What we collect</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Your account:</strong> your username, email address, password (stored only as a one-way hash), and any profile details you add, such as an avatar, website, location, occupation or interests.</li>
  <li><strong>Facebook login:</strong> the forum used to offer Facebook login. For accounts created that way we still keep the Facebook user ID and name we received then. Facebook login is no longer available, and we don't receive anything new from Facebook.</li>
  <li><strong>What you post:</strong> forum topics and replies, which are public.</li>
  <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> the IP address and time of your recent logins, a login cookie, and standard server logs.</li>
</ul>

<h2>How we use it</h2>
<p>We use this information only to run the forum: to log you in, show your posts and profile, keep out spam, and fix problems with the site. We don't sell it or use it for advertising.</p>

<h2>Who else handles it</h2>
<p>The site is hosted on Railway. We use Google reCAPTCHA on sign-up to block spam, and error-tracking services that may receive technical details when something goes wrong. Each handles data under its own privacy policy.</p>

<h2>Deleting your data</h2>
<p>You can ask us to delete your account and its data at any time. See <%= link_to 'how to delete your data', data_deletion_path %>.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about this policy can be sent to <%= mail_to privacy_email %>.</p>
